  "source": [
    {
      "kind": "client",
      "evidence": "Global.Text 130341 'Brugo's Fishing Spot' (title), 130342 (card), objective 130377; icon 11418."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Starter at [-1911.49, -36.73, -637.76]: BJX fork Battles.lua:83 (Npcs.json Id 46256, chugawug_m_02.adr). (R) the fork's own placement, not a captured one. Region The Wilds, place The Wilds."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 91 ('Brugo's Fishing Spot (the live random encounter: selfish Brugo's fishing hole)'): scene sg_random_encounter_creek, entry, exit, 3 waves, 9 spawns ({'Bandit Patrolman': 5, 'Thugawug Stomper': 3, 'Brugo': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1243 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sg_random_encounter_creek has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 60 coins / 220 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) rc-0137 prize wheel (2026-11-12): 'Brugo's Fishing Spot' has no wheel of its own on the wiki; the wiki's item pages put its prize wheel with 'Frostfang Caverns' (Ninja's Jagged Scythe of Shuriken Storm; Wizard's Jewel Wand of Firestorm; Warrior’s Double Axe of Earthquake; Medic's Megasaw of Alarm), so it spins that wheel, from fandom 'Frostfang Caverns' (revision 49145), one per combat job, and 97 coins. The same pages also name Prince of Low Tide!, frostfang_caverns, prince_of_low_tide."
    }
  ]
